-- ============================================================
-- OSFishing — CONSOLIDATED SCHEMA
-- ============================================================
-- Complete database structure and seed content in one file.
-- Generated by replaying all migrations in dependency order and
-- dumping the verified result.
--
-- To build a fresh database:
--     mysql -u <user> -p <database> < schema.sql
--
-- This supersedes replaying the individual *_migration.sql files,
-- which are retained as history. Three of them do not replay cleanly
-- against a fresh database and were corrected while producing this file:
--
--   * admin_migration.sql       re-adds players.is_admin, already in the
--                               base schema (applied here as idempotent)
--   * butcher_migration.sql     used columns fish_species_id/affinity_weight
--                               (real names: fish_id/affinity) and joined a
--                               table, fish_spot_availability, that does not
--                               exist; rewritten against fish_water_types
--   * missing_columns_migration.sql
--                               NEW — adds quests.quest_group, quests.quest_tier
--                               and bait_types.min_level, which were added
--                               directly to the old live database and never
--                               captured in any committed migration
--
-- Order also matters: quest_data.sql inserts explicit quest ids 1-12 and must
-- run before repeatable_quest_migration.sql, which relies on auto-increment.
--
-- Contains no player data. Register the first account through the web portal.
--
-- Known pre-existing issue, NOT fixed here: includes/Tournament.php queries
-- columns (name, metric, spot_id, region_name, grid_name, start_time,
-- end_time, status, created_by) that do not match the tournaments table
-- (title, scoring_type, starts_at, ends_at, ...). Tracked in CLAUDE.md.
-- ============================================================

